\title{sdpMig2: stochastic dynamic programming model of optimal bird migration}
\description{
Stochastic dynamic programming model of optimal migration on a network of sites (e.g. hexagons of a grid) between one wintering and one breeding site. Daily food gain at each site follows spring phenology (growing degree day jerk). Individuals decide each day to forage, with an optimal intensity, or to fly to another site, given their body condition and the date. Fitness is a terminal reward that depends on arrival at the breeding site within an arrival window around the local onset of spring and on body condition at arrival. The backward iteration computes the optimal policy; the forward simulation follows individuals under that policy, with stochastic food gain, predation, flight mortality and decision error. The model core is written in C++ via 'Rcpp' and 'RcppArmadillo'.
}
